 :adr/body "## Context\n\nClosing record for the 2026-09-10 session that moved the hermes bot fleet onto\napi.murakumo.cloud (adr-2609100300), established the model-max context\n(adr-2609100400), and then -- on owner instruction -- took chat inference off\ngad entirely.\n\nOwner instruction, given after being shown that gad had crashed under the\nraised context and stranded 41.5 GiB of its 48 GiB VRAM:\n\n    gad 以外で推論を進めたい. gad は動画生成にフォーカスさせたい\n\nwith the head context set to `-c 262144 --parallel 1`.\n\n## Decision\n\n**gad is video generation only.** `murakumo-ring.service` is stopped and\n`systemctl disable`d there, permanently and on purpose. `fleet.edn` already\nlabelled gad `:role \"comfy-render\"`, so this matches the repo's own declared\nintent rather than overriding it.\n\n**Chat inference is b70 and xavier.** b70's window was raised from 16,384 to\n32,768 per slot, keeping two slots.\n\n## What was done, and what each step measured\n\n| step | measured result |\n|---|---|\n| stop + disable `murakumo-ring` on gad | `inactive / disabled` |\n| reboot gad to reclaim stranded VRAM | VRAM used 41.8 GiB -> **0.6 GiB** of 48 |\n| ComfyUI's own view after reboot | `vram_free` 6.4 GiB -> **47.7 GiB** of 48 |\n| bot fleet during the reboot | unaffected; b70 served throughout |\n| b70 `--ctx-size` 32768 -> 65536, `--parallel 2` | **32,768 per slot x 2**, VRAM 22.2 of 31.9 GiB, verified serving |\n| cron runs after all of it | **32/32 ok** in 60 min, 21/21 in 30 min |\n\nThe reboot was affordable only because inference came off gad first. That\nordering was the point: the same reboot an hour earlier would have taken the\nwhole bot fleet down with it.\n\n## The owner's `-c 262144 --parallel 1` does not fit on b70, measured\n\nb70 has a **discrete 32 GiB Intel Arc Pro B70**. Its unit comment says the box\nhas 15 GiB with ~4 GiB available, and that is HOST ram -- the model and KV live\nin dedicated VRAM, and reading the host figure as the budget is what made this\nlook impossible at first. `dmesg` is the source:\n\n    xe 0000:03:00.0: [drm] VRAM[0]: Actual physical size 0x800000000   (32 GiB)\n\nAt `--ctx-size 32768` the server held 20.4 GiB of it; doubling to 65536 cost\nonly 1.8 GiB more, so KV is about 57 KiB/token, far cheaper than a first\nestimate of 150 KiB/token suggested. That made 262,144 look plausible.\n\nIt is not. `--ctx-size 262144 --parallel 1` was applied and **crashed on load**\n(`code=dumped, status=6/ABRT`); 262,144 tokens of KV is roughly 38 GiB against\na 32 GiB card once the 15.7 GiB of weights are resident. Reverted to the\nverified `--ctx-size 65536 --parallel 2` within about a minute, which is why\nthe fleet shows no errors across the window.\n\n**262,144 per slot exists nowhere in the pool now.** gad's two slots were the\nonly ones that reached it.\n\n## The blocker that remains, and it is not on the heads\n\nThe usable request envelope is still about **3,000 prompt tokens / 15 KB** --\nthe same as before any of this work:\n\n    15,000 chars   3,016 prompt tokens   HTTP 200\n    16,000 chars   --                    HTTP 502, no x-murakumo-route-head\n\nb70 really is serving 32,768 now; `/ready` reports `slot-context: 32768`. But\nthe pool's fit decision reads a **hand-maintained constant**, not the live\nprobe:\n\n    cloud-murakumo-api  src/local_murakumo/provider_catalog.cljc\n      :members [{:head \"b70\" :slots 2 :context 16384 ...}      <- really 32768\n                {:head \"gad\" :slots 2 :context 262144 ...}]    <- now disabled\n      :capacity-measured-at \"2026-09-07\"\n\nSo the router believes b70 caps at 16,384 and that gad still exists at\n262,144. Combined with the gateway counting **UTF-8 bytes as tokens** in\n`budgetRequest` (`src/model_token_limits.js`), anything past ~15 KB matches no\nhead and returns 502.\n\nNot changed here: it needs an edit and a production deploy of the Worker every\nbot depends on, and the owner was asked and had not answered when the session\nclosed.\n\n## Resume point\n\nThe next concrete step, in `orgs/network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api`:\n\n1. In `src/local_murakumo/provider_catalog.cljc` `:members`, set b70 to\n   `:context 32768` and remove the gad entry (or set its slots to 0). Read the\n   live values first rather than copying these: `curl -s\n   https://api.murakumo.cloud/ready | jq '.hosted-models'`.\n2. `npm test` (5 model-limit tests, plus the cljs/bundle/kotoba suites), then\n   `npm run deploy`.\n3. Re-measure the envelope. Expect roughly 8k tokens with the table fixed, and\n   roughly 32k if the byte-as-token reserve in `budgetRequest` is also\n   corrected -- that reserve is deliberately conservative and documented as\n   such, so changing it is its own risk decision.\n\nVerification command for the consumer side, unchanged:\n\n    nbb scripts/hermes-murakumo-api.cljs --verify     # 0 clean / 1 findings / 2 refused\n\n## Open, named\n\n- `/ready` answers `ok: true` while the primary head is dead, demoting it to\n  `degraded: [\"primary-unavailable\"]` inside the payload. That is why the\n  original outage went unnoticed for so long. Unfixed; it is in\n  cloud-murakumo-api.\n- `murakumo-ring` can strand itself again on any box: a stop that exceeds\n  `TimeoutStopSec` lands it in `failed`, and `Restart=on-failure` does not\n  recover that state.\n- 31 cron jobs name a `workdir` under the retired `~/.gftd`; the `.itonami`\n  equivalents do not exist either (removed worktrees). 24 of them last ran OK\n  because a job with a missing workdir falls back to its profile directory.\n- `com.gftd.hermes-budget-guard.plist` still logs to `~/.gftd/`, recreating the\n  retired directory every 5 minutes.\n- OpenRouter had $10.00 left of $2,386 and remains the fallback lane.\n\n## Files\n\n- `scripts/hermes-murakumo-api.cljs` -- `--verify` guidance corrected: it used\n  to tell the reader to restart `murakumo-ring` on gad, which is now the\n  opposite of the decision. 41 self-test assertions.\n- `90-docs/adr/2609100400` -- amended in place with what changed and why, per\n  the workspace rule that a document shows the current state.\n"}]
